{
  "q1_accurate": [
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "Batch (file: batch.go)", "note": "composed_by gave the complete direct-holder list I cited in Step 1: indexedBatch batch.go:488, batchIter batch.go:1761, commitQueue commit.go:25, iteratorBatchState iterator.go:392, plus second-hop commitPipeline commit.go:216, iterAllocCommon db.go:962, Iterator iterator.go:200, replay/metamorphic holders"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "note": "retained_via_interfaces was the core deliverable: 11 of its 14 rows I confirmed at source and cited (wal.recordQueueEntry RefCount, mergingIter/compact.Iter/invalidating/iterv2/keyspan InternalIterator rows, rangeKeyMasking as SpanMask and BoundLimitedBlockPropertyFilter, ConcurrencyLimitScheduler.db, bench.ycsb.db), each with the correct struct file:line"},
    {"tool": "sense_status", "query": "(none)", "note": "confirmed full index coverage and surfaced pebble.Batch as a key symbol with batchIter/commitQueue callers, correctly framing Step 1"}
  ],
  "q1_wrong": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "note": "row 'record.Writer via flusher, carrier bench.pebbleDB' was a false positive — record.NewWriter derives f from an io.Writer file, pebbleDB never lands there; row 'keyspan.SpanIterOptions via BlockPropertyFilter, carrier rangeKeyMasking' also refuted — scan_internal.go:1101 injects user-provided filters; and the list missed the flushableEntry/flushable-interface retainer (flushable.go:70 holding *flushableBatch that owns batch.data), which turned out to be a top-risk finding"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "write batch type callers build up writes before committing", "note": "did not return the pebble.Batch type definition itself (top hits were BatchCommitStats, DB, bench constants); sense_status's key_symbols is what actually pointed me at batch.go:240"}
  ],
  "q2_fallbacks": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "retained_via_interfaces rows are explicitly unverified about which satisfier the field holds at runtime and carry no injection-site line, so every row required grep/read to find the actual construction site (db.go:908 for wal.RefCount, open.go:446 for the scheduler, db.go:1435/1577 for the iterator stack, ycsb.go:316 for bench)"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "fallback": "read", "missing": "no goroutine-boundary information at all — the go d.flush() at compaction.go:1389, stopper.runAsync sites in wal/failover_writer.go:611/721/869/891, and periodicGranter at compaction_scheduler.go:306 all had to be recovered by grep to build the Step 3 risk ranking"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "pebble.Batch", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "retention through a raw []byte alias (newFlushableBatch taking ownership of batch.data, batch.go:2007) is invisible to the interface-retention analysis; I found it only by reading commitWrite"}
  ],
  "q3_hints": [
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query_before": "Batch (file: batch.go)", "query_after": "sense_blast pebble.Batch", "hint": "next_steps in the sense_graph response said '67 callers reach this - run sense_blast for full change impact and what holds it (retained_via_interfaces, holders that keep it behind an interface and never name it)', which is exactly the tool call that produced the audit's core row set"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query_before": "pebble.Batch (trusting rows as-is)", "query_after": "grep/read verification of each carrier's injection site", "hint": "retained_note text 'Unverified, and the only unverified part: which satisfier the field holds at runtime' made me verify every row at source, which caught the two false-positive carriers"}
  ],
  "q4_value": "The retained_via_interfaces list from sense_blast on pebble.Batch: a near-complete enumeration of interface-laundered retainers (the whole point of the audit) with correct struct file:lines and containment chains, spanning packages (wal, internal/compact, internal/keyspan, bench) I could not have connected to Batch by grepping for the type name.",
  "q5_improve": "Attach the concrete injection/assignment site (file:line where the carrier value is stored into the interface field) to each retained_via_interfaces row — that verification consumed most of my session's grep/read calls and is also where the two false-positive carriers would have self-evidently failed.",
  "score": 9,
  "score_rationale": "The retained_via_interfaces set (Q1) is exactly the class of result grep cannot produce — structs that never name Batch, found across five packages in one call — but the two refuted carriers, one missed retainer (flushableEntry), and the per-row injection-site verification I had to do by grep (Q2) keep it at the bottom of the 9-10 band."
}

